{
  "_about": [
    "The Dungeon Journal's factions, kept by hand; Tools/build_factions.py turns this into one Lua",
    "file per faction in DungeonJournal/Data/Factions, its rewards from the game's item tables",
    "(every item that needs a standing with the faction). tab is the Journal's tab it is listed",
    "under: reputation, or pvp for a battleground's faction (side Alliance or Horde: only that",
    "side sees it). id is the game's faction ID. zone is where its quartermaster is. dungeons are",
    "the Journal's keys of the dungeons and raids where the reputation is earned, linked both",
    "ways. group puts factions under one title in the list (the Steamwheedle Cartel's four",
    "towns). new marks a faction new in WoW Forever. name, when given, replaces the game's.",
    "side on a reputation faction (a city) lists it only for that side.",
    "unreleased marks a faction whose raids WoW Forever has not announced: listed apart, closed.",
    "alsoIn names other zones it is earned in: there too, the map (M) shows it beside it.",
    "By hand, on top of the game's tables: a faction's \"add\" list adds rewards they do not",
    "have yet, e.g. { \"item\": 272063, \"standing\": \"Honored\", \"price\": \"9g 1s 14c\",",
    "\"note\": \"on the PTR\" } (price and note optional), and its \"remove\" list drops item IDs",
    "they have wrong. Its \"turnins\" list names its repeatable hand-ins, which the game's",
    "tables do not have (a quest's rewards come from the server): { \"name\": the quest's,",
    "\"quests\": its IDs (one per side), \"rep\": what one hand-in gives, \"takes\": [[item ID,",
    "count], ...] }, from the quest's page on Wowhead Forever. See DungeonJournal/README.md,",
    "Adding things."
  ],
